              delivered ending is exactly one of success, failure, notSent and unknown, an Attempt that ever ended
              unknown never delivers a definite failure, and a never-sent Attempt ends only NotSent or unknown Restored
              at a boot (WriteLanes I3); every request of one Attempt carries one idempotency key and one input
              (WriteLanes I6); each turn publishes at most once and an accepted transition exactly once (Turn I9); a
              refused turn publishes one issue-only snapshot and no Turn report (Turn I14); after Runtime disposal
              starts no commit or read is invoked (Actors I30).
            - Each rule has a named planted fault in `tests/faults.ts` that turns it red (none exists today for
              WriteLanes I3, I15, I16, Turn I9 or Actors I30).
            - The reload sweep runs every fixture story's `Story.Step` array with a reload inserted at each position
              (`run({ steps })`) and applies the rules. A variant fails only for a rule breach, never for a script
              reason; script faults a reload can cause (a release with nothing held, an unused hold) are skipped and
              counted. A second variant inserts `reload({ reattach: false })` (@plan.Pending D10), so a boot that fails
              to wake owed identities shows.
            - `nub run faults` catches every named fault, the 23 there today included.
