    T67
        title       The hand cases run as Story tests and the bridge is gone
        status      done
        priority    high
        blocked_by  [@T63, @T64]
        description
            Port the 81 cases under `tests/bridge/cases/` to Story tests by Spec area, and delete the bridge.

            **Why now:** two test styles in one tree is how a private harness comes back. Core work (@task.V3.T54) waits
            on this.

            **Read first:** code:wiki/plans/flow/references/proposals/test-system-2026-11-15.md (section 5 and Appendix
            A), the bridge's `tests/bridge/cases/write-lanes/payment-endings.test.ts` (deleted by this Task;
            at `3e1fb97b`).

            **Approach:** the pay, cells, sync and sign-in fixtures in the four-file shape first, each in its own folder
            (cells moves out of `fixtures/pay/`) and following the transfers fixture of @task.V3.T63 (`Fake.server` with
            a port fake Layer, chained Stories, no handler closures). Then one Spec area per commit, each commit
            deleting the bridge files it replaces. The five `-usual` and five `-stress` scripts on the branch
            `draft/story-slice` (`draft/workloads/`) become each fixture's usual and long Stories, rewritten in the
            chained form.

            The old `answer` and `ack` words map onto the Plan's words, so a server never answers against its own truth:

            | Old | New |
            | --- | --- |
            | `answer ok` | the endpoint's handler, unchanged |
            | `answer fail` | a control that makes the handler decline (`Bank.limit({ cents: 0 })`) |
            | `answer lost` | `drop({ at: "request" })`: the handler never runs |
            | `answer lostButLanded` | `drop({ at: "response" })`: the handler runs, the answer is lost |
            | `answer failButLanded` | a control whose handler applies the change and returns the failure |
            | `answer never` | `hold({ at })` never released |
            | `ack` | `Fake.storage` `hold` set before the write (in `world`), then `release`; an unheld write lands |

            A case no mapping expresses is listed as dropped with its reason, for the user's read.

            May change: `fixtures/`, `tests/`, `vite.config.ts` (the bridge's lint exemption). Evidence: this
            Task's comments.

            False pass: a ported test that asserts less than its case did → caught by comparing asserted values case by
            case, and by `nub run faults`.
        acceptance
